# DTF tier manifest: inline-scan-fail-open-2954  (#2954)
# Profile-set: filesystem + trivy scanner. Needs the bundled Grype engine
# (seeded CVE-DB) AND outbound pypi.org access, same as
# inline-scan-proxy-pypi-2954.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS (#2954, Part 4 — fail-open must be LOUD, never silent):
#   The default proxy_scan_action is fail-open (latency-first): a first pull of
#   an unknown digest is served immediately WHILE an async Grype scan populates
#   the digest-keyed verdict, and the NEXT pull of that digest is blocked if the
#   verdict is vulnerable. Fail-open must never be a silent #1274-style gap:
#   the served-unscanned response carries `X-AK-Scan: pending` (plus a warn +
#   audit signal server-side).
#
# Discriminating oracle (oracle.sh), fail-open on a CVE wheel:
#   * First pull  -> 200 with `X-AK-Scan: pending` (served, async scan kicked).
#       Pre-#2954: 200 with NO X-AK-Scan header (silent unscanned serve) -> FAIL.
#   * After the async verdict lands -> a `vulnerable` proxy_scan_results row.
#   * Second pull -> 403 scan_blocked (the async verdict now blocks the digest).
#       Pre-#2954: still 200 -> FAIL.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin login + setup + repeated pulls + a short poll
# for the async verdict.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem scanners.trivy"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
NEEDS_INTERNET="true"
